# FABLE-SONNET-RECEIVE-RENAME-20260924-166 commit 3 (D-48): the author on the mixed-type case
# (verbatim LMX_blog/2026-09-25.md): "главное чтобы так можно было сделать и (int: x 1; char: x
# (x + 2)) читался правильно" -- a DIFFERENT-typed repeated declaration needs its initialiser
# value carried across types (the ported lingvamyxa_prev converters, S7), not a C cast and not
# implicit numeric widening. That port has not landed, so this is a located refusal.
fn: test () int
    int: x 1
    char: x (x + 2)
    return: 0
end: test

return: test()
